decision either way. Root 'system' with btop installed, and 'terminal' with Alacritty: assert which row is first.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1425}],"title":"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app"},{"forClaim":10,"rationale":"For root 'tu' with one matching app, assert the boundary count and position. This turns the divider change into a decided, pinned behaviour.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1406}],"title":"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present"},{"forClaim":11,"rationale":"With 200 synthetic app rows, record the index of the first menu row for one-letter queries and assert a bound the maintainer accepts.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"title":"Burial at scale"},{"forClaim":12,"rationale":"Enumerate tiers x kinds x realistic depth/order and assert app max < menu min. It fails loudly if a tier >= 98 is added.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377}],"title":"Tier-gap invariant property test"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #12223 (ax1g) ranks installed apps above menu entries in menu search (mirror commit 11b839fb, identical to upstream head b74292ac). `searchScore` changes the app bias from -5 to -100 (MenuModel.js:377). That exceeds every match tier, so any matching app outranks any matching menu entry. `rebuildDisplay` pins matching app rows above the current menu's rows and re-derives the divider (Menu.qml:695-713). Upstream also edits test/shell.d/menu-test.sh: a new `vsc` test and an inverted cross-tier assertion. The later mirror commits are our proof work, not upstream's: SJ7P/TKDP rewritten to the PR's intent, rebuildDisplay witnesses, the #10340 test in reporter-expectation mode, citation re-points, REVIEW-261001-EAD8/-ER1B, a KI note and trace re-reviews.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** The engine measured the changed decisions: 2/2 covered, 0 uncovered lines or outcomes. The run ingested 56 test results: 56 passed, 0 failed. I re-ran both node suites at a8d9ba21: 30 passed, 1 unrelated skip (#10601 needs Qt). I also ran base 87c3ca68 vs head `rebuildDisplay`. For `vsc`, VS Code now comes first. For `system`, btop sits above the exact-label System menu. At root `tu`, the direct/deeper divider moves below the app.\n\n**Compatibility.** There are 4 unapproved compat changes, each a compat_change_unapproved disclosure that prevents ready. Two are test_diff changes: the replay MC/DC values and the #10340 test rewrite. Two are removed-behaviour items in that test's helper. All four follow the PR's stated intent. The 28 compat_auditor_note disclosures (7 per finding) are notes, not approvals; only a human reviewer can approve. The differential ran 213 inputs with no difference. Its harness does not exercise search ranking, so it is no evidence about ranking.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Should a keyword-only app beat an exact-label menu entry? (2) Is dropping the direct/deeper divider when an app matches intended? (3) Can many apps bury menu entries?\n\n**Traceability.** SJ7P and TKDP were modified. 39 more requirements are code_changed through file-level traces. No spec-gap candidates; effects were not analyzed, so uncodified connections could not be detected.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** Nothing pre-existing prevents readiness. No check failed, and 13 checks were skipped by configuration. Readiness is not_assessed. The next decision is human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved), by a reviewer."}
